      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In this case, a statistical method such as Z-score analysis or standard deviation calculation can help you identify noise in the data. The Z-score measures the number of standard deviations an item is from the mean, which in your case, could indicate anomalies. By applying a threshold (e.g., 2 or 3 standard deviations above the mean) and flagging items that don't meet this threshold, you can signal that these expenses are unlikely to be due to random variation or minor errors.",
